Draw rounded corners as continuous corners, as Apple does, in the Metal quad SDF: a corner of radius r starts 1.528 r from the corner and is a superellipse in that box, its exponent chosen to cross the diagonal where the circle does (back to the circle when the box must shrink, as in a pill); gradient-normalised so antialiasing keeps one pixel. Experiment for Quiet.md's design system (R 14); Windows and wgpu shaders unchanged.

